# ── play-testing harness (test/) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# playwright-core is a TEST-ONLY dependency (14MB) and must never ship with the
# book, which has no build step and no runtime dependencies at all. It drives the
# Edge already installed on the machine, so no browser is downloaded.
# Install it with:  cd test && npm install playwright-core
test/node_modules/
# Screenshots the play scripts write for eyeballing a run; regenerated every time.
test/shots/

# ── LBD games ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev-only dependencies. Neither game needs node_modules at RUNTIME (LBD 2 loads
# a vendored js/vendor/gsap.min.js; LBD 1 is a single inline index.html), so 28MB
# of it should not ship with the book.
LBD/*/node_modules/

# HISTORY — why the games once deployed as 404s, so it is not repeated:
# each game folder used to carry its OWN .git, which made `git add` stage it as an
# embedded repository instead of its files. Commit 41e0986 recorded exactly two
# entries for LBD/ — both mode 160000 (gitlink) — so a clone or Vercel build got
# two EMPTY game folders and both game pages 404'd. Ignoring the nested .git does
# NOT help; git decides on the presence of .git on disk, not on ignore rules.
# The nested repos have been removed and the 144 real game files are tracked here.
# Their history lives on their own remotes if either is ever needed again:
#   github.com/yuvrajsingh-alt/THE-GLASS-HALF-FULL
#   github.com/harshvishnu4-cpu/Glass-Half-full-LBD-2-
# If a game folder is ever re-cloned INTO this repo, delete its .git again.
